---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Find the one bad request" hint="20,000 simulated requests, scaled up to a day of 100 million traces. About 1 in 70 is slow or failed, and one of them is the checkout a customer is complaining about. Choose what to keep and see whether you can still find it.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Start with the default, <b>keep 10% at the start of the request</b>, no tail sampling: about <b>99 GB a day</b>, and only <b>28 of the 299</b> slow or failed traces survive. The customer's request was thrown away before anyone knew it was bad, so you <b>cannot find it</b>.</li>
    <li>Switch to <b>100% head sampling with tail sampling on</b> and a 10 s wait: about <b>23 GB a day</b> (2% of the 100% cost), <b>298 of 299</b> bad traces kept and the customer's request found with all 24 spans. The price is a collector holding about <b>12,000 traces</b> in memory.</li>
    <li>Cut the wait to <b>1 s</b>: the sampler decides before the slow root span and the late spans arrive. Only <b>58 of 299</b> bad traces are kept, nearly all of those <b>incomplete</b>, and the customer's request is lost. At <b>5 s</b> it is kept but without its error span, so you see slow and not why. At <b>60 s</b> nothing is incomplete, but the buffer is about <b>5.7 times larger</b>.</li>
    <li>Now put <b>head sampling back to 10% with tail sampling on</b>: the sampler is cheap (about 1,500 traces in memory), yet it only sees the 10% that survived, so 90% of the bad traces are gone before it can look. Tail sampling needs the head to keep everything.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg tcb" data-tcb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Head sampling (decided in the app) <select class="pg-in" data-head>
        <option value="1">keep 100%</option>
        <option value="0.1" selected>keep 10%</option>
        <option value="0.01">keep 1%</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Tail sampling in the collector <select class="pg-in" data-tail>
        <option value="off" selected>off</option>
        <option value="on">on: keep errors, slow traces and 1% of the rest</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Buffer wait before deciding <select class="pg-in" data-wait>
        <option value="1">1 s</option>
        <option value="5">5 s</option>
        <option value="10" selected>10 s</option>
        <option value="30">30 s</option>
        <option value="60">60 s</option>
      </select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Storage per day</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Bad traces kept (errors and slow)</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Incomplete traces kept</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Tail sampler memory</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b5><h3>The customer's failed checkout</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o5></span><span class="pg-note" data-n5></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Assumptions: 100 million traces a day (1,157 a second), 20 spans per trace on average and 500 bytes stored per span, so 100% is about 1 TB a day. A trace is bad if one span has an error or the root span took over 2 s. Spans reach the collector 0.1 to 1.5 s after they end, and 8% of traces have an async hop (a queue consumer) that ends up to 40 s after the start. The tail sampler decides once, at the first span plus the wait, from the spans it has seen; later spans of that trace are dropped. It keeps 1% of normal traces as a baseline. It needs a collector that gets every span of a trace, for example by routing on the trace id, and holds about 2 KB of memory per buffered span. The customer's request is a 6 s trace of 24 spans whose error comes from an async worker 9.5 s in, and it is not among the 10% or 1% that head sampling keeps.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-tcb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const N = 20000; const WINDOW = 200; const PROD_TRACES = 100e6; const SPAN_BYTES = 500; const MEM_PER_SPAN = 2000; const SLOW = 2; const PLANT = 7777;
    const RATE = { error: 0.005, errorOrSlow: 0.015, async: 0.08 }; // share of traces with an error, an error or slowness (so 1% slow), an async tail span
    const DUR = { slow: [2.5, 9], error: [0.1, 3], normal: [0.05, 0.9] }; // root duration in s: [base, random range]
    const SPANS = { min: 8, range: 25 }; // spans per trace: 8 to 32
    const CHILD_END = { min: 0.15, range: 0.85 }; // a child span ends at 15% to 100% of the root duration
    const ARRIVAL_DELAY = { min: 0.1, range: 1.4 }; // s between a span ending and reaching the collector
    const ASYNC_END = { min: 5, range: 35 }; // s, when the async worker span ends
    const PLANT_TRACE = { dur: 6, spans: 24, asyncEnd: 9, asyncDelay: 0.5 }; // the one request the reader has to find
    const UINT32 = 4294967296; const BASELINE_SALT = 99991; // second independent hash per trace
    const BASELINE_KEEP = 0.01; // tail sampler also keeps 1% of ordinary traces
    const DAY_S = 86400;
    const BUFFERED_SPANS = 20; // average spans held per buffered trace
    const GOOD_SHARE_PCT = 95; const STORAGE_WARN_B = 5e11; const INCOMPLETE_WARN = 0.1; // card thresholds
    // integer hash (murmur3-style finalizer)
    const mix = (x: number) => { let h = Math.imul(x ^ 0x9e3779b9, 2654435761) >>> 0; h ^= h >>> 15; h = Math.imul(h, 2246822519) >>> 0; h ^= h >>> 13; return h >>> 0; };
    type Span = { end: number; arr: number; err: boolean; root: boolean };
    type Trace = { id: number; error: boolean; slow: boolean; n: number; spans: Span[]; h: number; b: number; first: number };
    // Numerical Recipes LCG
    let seed = 1234567; const rnd = () => ((seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296) / 4294967296);
    const traces: Trace[] = [];
    for (let id = 0; id < N; id++) {
      const start = rnd() * WINDOW; const r = rnd();
      const error = id === PLANT || r < RATE.error; const slow = !error && r < RATE.errorOrSlow;
      const dur = id === PLANT ? PLANT_TRACE.dur : slow ? DUR.slow[0] + rnd() * DUR.slow[1] : error ? DUR.error[0] + rnd() * DUR.error[1] : DUR.normal[0] + rnd() * rnd() * DUR.normal[1];
      const n = id === PLANT ? PLANT_TRACE.spans : SPANS.min + Math.floor(rnd() * SPANS.range);
      const hasAsync = id === PLANT || rnd() < RATE.async; const errAt = Math.floor(rnd() * n);
      const spans: Span[] = [];
      for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) {
        let end = k === 0 ? dur : dur * (CHILD_END.min + CHILD_END.range * rnd()); let delay = ARRIVAL_DELAY.min + rnd() * ARRIVAL_DELAY.range; let err = error && k === errAt;
        if (hasAsync && k === n - 1) { end = id === PLANT ? PLANT_TRACE.asyncEnd : ASYNC_END.min + rnd() * ASYNC_END.range; delay = id === PLANT ? PLANT_TRACE.asyncDelay : ARRIVAL_DELAY.min + rnd() * ARRIVAL_DELAY.range; err = error && (id === PLANT || k === errAt || errAt === n - 1); }
        if (id === PLANT) err = k === n - 1;
        spans.push({ end, arr: start + end + delay, err, root: k === 0 });
      }
      traces.push({ id, error, slow, n, spans, h: mix(id) / UINT32, b: mix(id + BASELINE_SALT) / UINT32, first: Math.min(...spans.map((s) => s.arr)) });
    }
    const errTotal = traces.filter((t) => t.error).length; const slowTotal = traces.filter((t) => t.slow).length;
    function run(head: number, tail: boolean, wait: number) {
      let kept = 0; let keptSpans = 0; let errKept = 0; let slowKept = 0; let incomplete = 0; const ev: number[][] = [];
      let plant = { kept: false, stored: 0, n: 0, hasErr: false };
      for (const t of traces) {
        if (!(t.h < head)) continue;
        let stored = t.n; let keep = true; let hasErr = true;
        if (tail) {
          const dec = t.first + wait; ev.push([t.first, 1], [dec, -1]);
          const seen = t.spans.filter((s) => s.arr <= dec); const root = seen.find((s) => s.root);
          hasErr = seen.some((s) => s.err); keep = hasErr || (root !== undefined && root.end > SLOW) || t.b < BASELINE_KEEP; stored = seen.length;
        }
        if (!keep) continue;
        kept++; keptSpans += stored; if (t.error) errKept++; if (t.slow) slowKept++; if (stored < t.n) incomplete++;
        if (t.id === PLANT) plant = { kept: true, stored, n: t.n, hasErr };
      }
      let cur = 0; let peak = 0; ev.sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0] || a[1] - b[1]); for (const e of ev) { cur += e[1]; peak = Math.max(peak, cur); }
      const perDay = PROD_TRACES / N;
      return { kept, errKept, slowKept, incomplete, bytes: keptSpans * perDay * SPAN_BYTES, prodPeak: peak * (PROD_TRACES / DAY_S) / (N / WINDOW), plant };
    }
    const sizeText = (b: number) => (b >= 1e12 ? `${(b / 1e12).toFixed(1)} TB` : b >= 1e10 ? `${Math.round(b / 1e9)} GB` : `${(b / 1e9).toFixed(1)} GB`);
    const pct = (f: number) => (f > 0 && f < 0.01 ? '<1%' : `${Math.round(100 * f)}%`);
    const count = (n: number) => Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-US');
    const full = run(1, false, 0).bytes;
    let queued = false;
    function draw() {
      queued = false;
      const head = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-head]').value); const tail = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-tail]').value === 'on'; const wait = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-wait]').value);
      q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-wait]').disabled = !tail;
      const r = run(head, tail, wait); const bad = errTotal + slowTotal; const badKept = r.errKept + r.slowKept; const share = Math.round((100 * badKept) / bad);
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = `${sizeText(r.bytes)} a day`; q('[data-n1]').textContent = `${pct(r.bytes / full)} of keeping everything (${sizeText(full)})`;
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = `${badKept} of ${bad} (${share}%)`; q('[data-n2]').textContent = `${r.errKept} of ${errTotal} errors, ${r.slowKept} of ${slowTotal} slow`;
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = r.kept ? `${r.incomplete} of ${r.kept}` : 'none kept'; q('[data-n3]').textContent = tail ? 'kept, but some spans arrived after the decision' : 'the decision is in the trace context, so every span is stored';
      const memBytes = r.prodPeak * BUFFERED_SPANS * MEM_PER_SPAN;
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = tail ? `${count(r.prodPeak)} traces (${memBytes >= 1e9 ? `${(memBytes / 1e9).toFixed(1)} GB` : `${Math.round(memBytes / 1e6)} MB`})` : '0';
      q('[data-n4]').textContent = tail ? `at the busiest moment, across all collectors, waiting ${wait} s each` : 'no buffering: the app decided before sending anything';
      const p = r.plant; const found = p.kept && p.hasErr && p.stored === p.n;
      q('[data-o5]').textContent = !p.kept ? 'not stored' : found ? `found, all ${PLANT_TRACE.spans} spans` : p.hasErr ? `kept, ${p.stored} of ${p.n} spans` : `kept, error span missing (${p.stored} of ${p.n})`;
      q('[data-n5]').textContent = !p.kept ? (tail && head === 1 ? 'dropped by the sampler: it looked ordinary at decision time' : 'thrown away before anyone knew it was bad') : found ? 'search error=true or the trace id and open it' : 'you see that it was slow, not why';
      const good = share >= GOOD_SHARE_PCT;
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b1]').style.setProperty('--c', r.bytes > STORAGE_WARN_B ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--accent)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b2]').style.setProperty('--c', good ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b3]').style.setProperty('--c', r.incomplete > INCOMPLETE_WARN * r.kept ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--accent)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b4]').style.setProperty('--c', 'var(--accent)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b5]').style.setProperty('--c', found ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); out.classList.toggle('bad', !found);
      out.textContent = found
        ? (tail ? `An engineer can find it. The sampler held the trace for ${wait} s, saw the error and kept all ${PLANT_TRACE.spans} spans, and the whole day costs ${sizeText(r.bytes)} and about ${count(r.prodPeak)} buffered traces.` : `An engineer can find it, but only because everything is kept: ${sizeText(r.bytes)} a day, with every normal request stored too.`)
        : !p.kept ? (tail && head < 1 ? `Not findable. Head sampling dropped this request at ${Math.round(head * 100)}% before the tail sampler could see it, so tail sampling only rescued ${badKept} of ${bad} bad traces.` : tail ? `Not findable. With a ${wait} s wait the sampler decided before the root span or the late async error arrived, so the trace looked ordinary and was dropped.` : `Not findable. The request was chosen at random at the start, before it failed, so it was thrown away with ${100 - Math.round(head * 100)}% of everything else. Only ${share}% of bad traces survive.`)
          : `Half found: the trace was kept because it was slow, but the sampler decided after ${wait} s, before the error span from the async worker arrived. You can see the slowness and not the cause.`;
    }
    const schedule = () => { if (!queued) { queued = true; requestAnimationFrame(draw); } };
    root.addEventListener('input', schedule); root.addEventListener('change', schedule);
    draw();
  });
</script>
